@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-validity`
IMPORT `g2-second-schedule`
IMPORT `g2-conditions`
IMPORT `g2-tests-fixtures`

-- g2-tests-conditions.l4: tests of section 6.
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of s 6(a)(1) to (4) and (b), the Second Schedule and the readings registered in
-- g2-conditions.l4, BEFORE any module was run.  A failing assertion is a finding.  Readings not taken: g2-tests-red.l4.

GIVETH AN Applicant
`a grade 3 certificate holder with a conviction on record` MEANS
    Applicant WITH
        `the person` IS `the test person`
        `of full age` IS TRUE
        `an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
        `an Israeli resident` IS TRUE
        `record of offences` IS `a record showing criminal conviction` TRUE `criminal charge pending` FALSE `and disciplinary conviction` FALSE
        `licences held` IS EMPTY
        `certificates held` IS LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`
        `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
        `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
        `completed a study programme that includes the complement course` IS FALSE
        `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch` IS FALSE
        `periods of work on cooling systems` IS EMPTY
        `holds a valid electrician licence of a kind listed in the Electricity Regulations` IS FALSE
        `holds a valid working-at-height approval` IS FALSE

§ `Tests — s 6(a)(1) to (3): the personal conditions`

-- (1) an adult; (2) an Israeli citizen or an Israeli resident; (3) no conviction and no pending indictment for a criminal offence
-- that makes the applicant unfit in the Registrar's opinion.
-- src:85 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} הוא בגיר;
-- src:86 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} הוא אזרח ישראלי או תושב ישראל;
-- src:87 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} הוא לא הורשע ולא תלוי ועומד נגדו כתב אישום בעבירה פלילית שמפאת מהותה, חומרתה או נסיבותיה אין הוא ראוי, לדעת הרשם, להיות בעל רישיון;
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(1) — the applicant is of full age` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` `a clean record`))
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(1) — the applicant is of full age` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` FALSE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` `a clean record`))
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` FALSE `, with the record` `a clean record`))
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` FALSE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` `a clean record`))
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` `a clean record`))
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` FALSE `, resident` FALSE `, with the record` `a clean record`))

-- (3): the opinion matters only where the record shows a conviction or a pending indictment.
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` (`a record showing criminal conviction` TRUE `criminal charge pending` FALSE `and disciplinary conviction` FALSE))) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` (`a record showing criminal conviction` TRUE `criminal charge pending` FALSE `and disciplinary conviction` FALSE))) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` (`a record showing criminal conviction` FALSE `criminal charge pending` TRUE `and disciplinary conviction` FALSE))) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` (`a record showing criminal conviction` FALSE `criminal charge pending` TRUE `and disciplinary conviction` FALSE))) FALSE
-- A disciplinary conviction is not "a criminal offence": it does not engage (3) even if the Registrar thinks it disqualifying.
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` (`a record showing criminal conviction` FALSE `criminal charge pending` FALSE `and disciplinary conviction` TRUE))) TRUE

§ `Tests — s 6(a)(4)(a) to (c): the three limbs, and the Second Schedule`

-- src:88 | {{ח:תתת|(4)}} מתקיים בו אחד התנאים שלהלן, והכול בהתאם לתנאים {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 2|שבתוספת השנייה}}:
-- src:89 | {{ח:תתתת|(א)}} הוא בעל תעודת גמר;
-- src:90 | {{ח:תתתת|(ב)}} הוא רשום במרשם ההנדסאים והטכנאים המוסמכים, בענף ובמדור קירור ומיזוג אוויר;
-- src:91 | {{ח:תתתת|(ג)}} הוא סיים בהצלחה לימודי השלמה, אם נדרשים כאמור {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 2|בטור ב׳ בתוספת השנייה}}, בהתאם להכשרתו ולניסיונו הקודמים כאמור {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 2|בטור א׳ בתוספת האמורה}}.
-- (a) holds a final certificate.
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)))
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`)))
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units`)))
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` (`an application on the usual day by` `an applicant with nothing`)
-- FC4: the youth school certificate counts (the Schedule calls it a final certificate); the alternative says it does not.
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a certificate of the Training Division vocational school for youth`)))
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(4)(a) (the youth school certificate not counted) — the applicant holds a final certificate` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a certificate of the Training Division vocational school for youth`)))
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(a) (the youth school certificate not counted) — the applicant holds a final certificate` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a certificate of the Training Division vocational school for youth`, `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)))
-- (b) registered in the register of technicians and practical engineers: a technician or a practical engineer, not a mechanical engineer.
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(b) — the applicant is registered as a technician or practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(b) — the applicant is registered as a technician or practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant registered as a practical engineer, programme completed being` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(4)(b) — the applicant is registered as a technician or practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` (`an application on the usual day by` `an applicant registered as a mechanical engineer`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(4)(b) — the applicant is registered as a technician or practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` (`an application on the usual day by` `an applicant with nothing`)

-- FC3: the training requirement is met when the training was completed in an approved programme, or the foreign qualification was recognised.
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4) with ss 19(b) and 19(c) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(4) with ss 19(b) and 19(c) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(4) with ss 19(b) and 19(c) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4) with ss 19(b) and 19(c) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4) (the programme's approval not a condition) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met` TRUE FALSE

-- (c) completed complementary studies, if required.  Where column B asks for training, it needs the training requirement; else TRUE.
-- The default item of Part A (no prior training) asks for training or a 3-unit certificate.
#ASSERT `Second Schedule — column B asks the applicant for training or complementary studies` (`an application on the usual day by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests`
-- A 3-unit holder seeking grade 1: A1(2), the certificate itself, asks nothing further.
#ASSERT NOT `Second Schedule — column B asks the applicant for training or complementary studies` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`))) `the commencement day in the tests`
-- B2, registered technician with the programme: no further requirements.
#ASSERT NOT `Second Schedule — column B asks the applicant for training or complementary studies` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE TRUE) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests`
-- B6, registered technician without the programme: up to 50 hours.
#ASSERT `Second Schedule — column B asks the applicant for training or complementary studies` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE FALSE) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests`

§ `Tests — s 6(a)(4) and (a): the conditions as a whole, route by route`

-- All three personal conditions hold in each of these; the route in (4) is the variable.  Arguments: opinion, completion, approval, recognition.
-- Route 1: no prior training (A1): training of up to 350 hours (completed in an approved programme) or a 3-unit certificate.
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing` `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing` `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing` `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- FC3: with the programme's approval not a condition the same facts qualify.
#ASSERT `s 6(a) (the programme's approval not a condition) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application on the usual day by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Foreign qualification recognised (s 19(c)): the training requirement is met without any course.
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing` `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` TRUE
-- Route 2: a 3-unit certificate holder seeking grade 1 meets A1(2) by the certificate itself: no course.
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- Seeking grade 2 (B3(3)): up to 100 hours are needed.
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
-- Route 3: B2, a registered technician with the programme: no further requirement; limb (b).
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE TRUE) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- B6, a registered technician without the programme: up to 50 hours.
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE FALSE) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE FALSE) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
-- C8, an engineer registered in the mechanical branch: up to 230 hours; limbs (a) and (b) fail, limb (c) carries it.
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` `an applicant registered as a mechanical engineer` `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` `an applicant registered as a mechanical engineer` `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
-- C2, a practical engineer with the programme: no further requirement; seeking grade 3.
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a practical engineer, programme completed being` TRUE TRUE) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE

-- D1 (2026-10-14, fork FS10): a grade 2 certificate holder seeking grade 2 has met item 1 by the certificate its course confers, so no course is asked of them (the first line, with the course completed, holds on either reading).
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE

-- The personal conditions still bind where (4) holds (route 1 with the course completed in an approved programme).
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` FALSE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` FALSE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` FALSE `, resident` FALSE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` (`a record showing criminal conviction` TRUE `criminal charge pending` FALSE `and disciplinary conviction` FALSE))) `with opinion` TRUE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` (`a record showing criminal conviction` TRUE `criminal charge pending` FALSE `and disciplinary conviction` FALSE))) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE

-- FC2, the alternative: "in accordance with the Second Schedule" asks nothing further of an applicant who meets a limb.
-- (i) The holder of a grade 1 certificate seeking a grade 1 licence: limb (a) holds, and since D1 (fork FS10) the Schedule asks nothing further of them either.
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`))) 
-- (the grade 1 holder is no longer a discriminating applicant for FC2: since D1 the default also qualifies them, see FS10 below; (ii) is the discriminating applicant)
#ASSERT `s 6(a) (the limbs of (4) alone) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`))) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (ii) A registered technician with the programme seeking a grade 1 licence: limb (b) holds, but Part A has no item for registrants, so the default item asks 350 hours or a 3-unit certificate.
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE TRUE) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) (the limbs of (4) alone) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant registered as a technician, programme completed being` TRUE TRUE)) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (iii) A practical engineer without the programme seeking a grade 2 licence: Part B has no item for practical engineers.
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a practical engineer, programme completed being` TRUE FALSE) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) (the limbs of (4) alone) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant registered as a practical engineer, programme completed being` TRUE FALSE) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (iv) An applicant with no limb at all fails on either reading.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) (the limbs of (4) alone) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application on the usual day by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- FC7 / FS10, repaired 2026-10-14 (defect D1).  The holder of the Division certificate of the grade sought has met item 1: the engine returns
-- item 1 alone for them, and the duty needs no course, no approved programme and no recognition.  Grade 1, grade 2 and grade 3 for the licence of the same grade:
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number`) (`training required for the licence sought` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests`) EQUALS LIST 1
-- The three functions named `(the certificate of the grade sought suffices)` were the alternative while the literal reading was the default; they now agree with the default.
#ASSERT `s 6(a) (the certificate of the grade sought suffices) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) (the certificate of the grade sought suffices) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) (the certificate of the grade sought suffices) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application on the usual day by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`))) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- It is narrow: a grade 1 certificate holder seeking grade 2 still needs the course of B3; an applicant with no certificate needs one.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) (the certificate of the grade sought suffices) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) (the certificate of the grade sought suffices) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application on the usual day by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) (the certificate of the grade sought suffices) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` (`an application on the usual day by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4) (the certificate of the grade sought) — the Division certificate that the course for a licence of the kind confers` `grade 2 licence` EQUALS `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`

-- FS10 and FS11, the neighbouring cases (D1, 2026-10-14).  Expected values come from the Schedule's own rows and the lead's ruling, not from the code.
-- Lower grade: the holder of a LOWER graded Division certificate still needs the course of the graded item that names it (B3 100 hours, C3 290, C4 240).
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
-- Higher grade (FS11): a certificate of a higher grade is not the one item 1 confers, so on the reading taken its holder is in the ungraded row (A3, B5(1): up to 50 hours).
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
-- FS11, the a fortiori alternative: a certificate of the grade sought or a higher grade meets item 1; a lower one still does not.
#ASSERT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with a Division certificate of a higher grade also meeting item 1 (FS11)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with a Division certificate of a higher grade also meeting item 1 (FS11)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with a Division certificate of a higher grade also meeting item 1 (FS11)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with a Division certificate of a higher grade also meeting item 1 (FS11)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with a Division certificate of a higher grade also meeting item 1 (FS11)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with a Division certificate of a higher grade also meeting item 1 (FS11)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- FS10, the literal alternative: the certificate of the grade sought is only a column A entry of the ungraded row, so its holder is asked for the course of A3, B5(1) or C6.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` TRUE `and recognition` FALSE
-- The literal reading asks for a course completed in an approved programme (FC3), as every course does.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- With the reading taken the function agrees with the default chain.
#ASSERT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 2 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a) under the reading` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with commencement day` `the commencement day in the tests` `, opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- The certificate stands in for the course, not for the person: the personal conditions of s 6(a)(1) to (3) still bind the holder.
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant who is adult` FALSE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` `a clean record`) `made on` `the usual application day`) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- s 6(a)(3) fails only where there is a conviction or a pending charge AND the Registrar is of the opinion that it makes the applicant unfit; the holder below has a conviction on record.
#ASSERT NOT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` `a grade 3 certificate holder with a conviction on record` `with opinion` TRUE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` `a grade 3 certificate holder with a conviction on record` `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` FALSE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE
-- No approved programme and no recognition is needed where the certificate is held: completion with approval FALSE still passes for the holder.
#ASSERT `the s 6(a) conditions hold for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `with opinion` FALSE `, completion` TRUE `, approval` FALSE `and recognition` FALSE


§ `Tests — s 6(a): the Registrar's duty, the fee (fork FC1), and the exported answer`

-- Applicant who meets every condition (route 1, grade 1): the duty arises when the fee was paid in full, not otherwise (taken).
-- The exported boolean `the Registrar must grant the licence` is the duty's trigger.
#ASSERT `the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application on the usual day for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application on the usual day for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application on the usual day for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- The scenario of the defect report: an adult citizen and resident with a clean record, programme approved by the Registrar, fee paid, who already holds the grade 3 certificate, seeking grade 3.
#ASSERT `the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- D1: the exported boolean for the holder of the Division certificate of the grade sought (grade 3, grade 3), with no course, no approval and no recognition: the duty arises when the fee was paid.
#ASSERT `the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application for a` `grade 3 licence` `by` (`an applicant holding only` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`)) `made on` `the usual application day`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- The duty itself, exercised with #TRACE (a deontic cannot be compared with EQUALS):
-- (1) conditions and fee: the Registrar who grants the licence sought, day 5, fulfils the duty;
#TRACE `s 6(a) — the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application on the usual day for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `grant the licence sought` `grade 1 licence` AT 5
-- (2) conditions and fee, nothing done: the duty stands, with no deadline (s 6(a) states none);
#TRACE `s 6(a) — the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application on the usual day for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- (3) the fee not paid: no duty arises (FC1 taken), so there is nothing to do;
#TRACE `s 6(a) — the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application on the usual day for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- (4) FC1's alternative, s 6(a) read without regulation 4: the same applicant with the fee unpaid is under the duty;
#TRACE `s 6(a) (read without regulation 4) — the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application on the usual day for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` `an applicant with nothing`) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- (5) a condition fails (not an adult): no duty.
#TRACE `s 6(a) — the Registrar must grant the licence` (`an application on the usual day for a` `grade 1 licence` `by` (`an applicant who is adult` FALSE `, citizen` TRUE `, resident` TRUE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) `the commencement day in the tests` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§ `Tests — s 6(b): the Minister's power to change the Second Schedule`

-- src:92 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} השר, באישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 2|התוספת השנייה}}.
-- With the committee's approval the power exists, and the Minister who uses it fulfils the rule; without approval no power arises.
#TRACE `s 6(b) — the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `change the Second Schedule by order` AT 3
#TRACE `s 6(b) — the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
#TRACE `s 6(b) — the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- FC6, the alternative: an order without the approval is a breach (here the Minister orders a change on day 3 without approval).
#TRACE `s 6(b) (an order without the approval is forbidden) — the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `change the Second Schedule by order` AT 3
#TRACE `s 6(b) (an order without the approval is forbidden) — the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `change the Second Schedule by order` AT 3
